  "locked": false,
  "title": "Tweak the exposure of cross-origin properties",
  "user": {
    "login": "domenic",
    "id": 617481,
    "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjYxNzQ4MQ==",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/617481?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/domenic",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/domenic",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/domenic/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/domenic/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/domenic/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/domenic/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/domenic/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/domenic/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/domenic/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/domenic/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/domenic/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "This contains two separate changes:\r\n\r\n* It makes all cross-origin properties that would normally be enumerable\r\n  on same-origin objects, enumerable also on WindowProxy and Location\r\n  objects (including when accessed same-origin). This includes\r\n  safelisted methods and attributes, browsing context name properties,\r\n  and browsing context index properties. The motivation for making them\r\n  non-enumerable seems to have been a mistaken impression that doing so\r\n  would prevent a cross-origin information leak.\r\n\r\n* It hides window names from [[OwnPropertyKeys]\\](), and thus\r\n  Object.keys(), Object.getOwnPropertyNames(), etc. This actually\r\n  prevents a cross-origin information leak.\r\n\r\nCloses #2753.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nMarking \"do not merge yet\" until we are aware of the web-compatibility implications of the latter change. Writing tests should help with that.",
